    "body": "@domenic Ah! Thanks for the explanation! I've updated the commit description. As for the test, I think the test sort of exposes an implementation detail of the two implementations. I'll have to think about a way to update the implementation and test.\r\n\r\n> I need some help understanding this, I'm struggling to understand the change request\r\n\r\nThe table the `onscrollend` is currently in states:\r\n\r\n> [...] that must be supported by all [Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#window) objects, as [event handler IDL attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-handler-idl-attributes) on the [Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#window) objects themselves, and with corresponding [event handler content attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-handler-content-attributes) and [event handler IDL attributes](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#event-handler-idl-attributes) exposed on all [body](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-body-element) and [frameset](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#frameset) elements that are owned by that [Window](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#window) object's [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-window):\r\n\r\nI don't think this should be the case for `onscrollend`.",
