    "created_at": "2023-05-16T03:23:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-05-16T03:23:33Z",
    "body": "So it is a bit weird to have `document.body` as a target even for standards documents. Do we really need to do this? And if so should the target be `document.body` or `document.scrollingElement`?\r\n\r\nIf the former, what if there's no `document.body`? And if the later, should it be the scrollingElement at the point the event is scheduled or dispatched? Because those might be different in quirks mode...\r\n\r\nI'd rather just have the event fire at `document` instead as Gecko is doing already but I'm curious to hear why firing at an element is useful.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
